<title>GERMANY: Escada says 1995/96 sales up, profit steady.</title>
<headline>Escada says 1995/96 sales up, profit steady.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>German women's retailer Escada AG said on Friday sales for its 1995/96 business year rose five percent to 1.23 billion marks ($741.4 million) but profit was steady at the prior year's level of 30.6 billion marks ($18.4 billion).</p>
<p>At its parent company, Escada said sales rose nine percent to 574 million marks and pre-tax profit rose 25 percent over the prior year's 19 million marks.</p>
<p>Escada also said business in the first months of its 1996/97 business year, which ends October 31, were going according to plan and that orders in hand so far were about equal with year-ago levels.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525 ($ = 1.659 German Marks)</p>
</text>
